# Section 23 — The end of wheels

The six numbered statements 23.1 … 23.6 of Chudnovsky–Robertson–Seymour–Thomas,
*The Strong Perfect Graph Theorem* (published/Annals version, printed pages
139–143).  Source of the verbatim quotations: `paper/pdf/S23_The_end_of_wheels.md`,
`## Numbered statements`.

**Three of the twelve main steps of the proof of 1.3 live here**: 23.2 discharges
1.8.9, 23.4 discharges 1.8.10 and 23.5 discharges 1.8.11 (see printed p. 13:
*"The twelve statements of 1.8 are proved in 5.1, 5.2, 9.6, 10.6, 13.4, 14.3,
16.3, 18.7, 23.2, 23.4, 23.5, and 24.1 respectively."*).

**23.6 is not a result of this paper.**  It is quoted by the authors from
reference [12] — M. Conforti, G. Cornuéjols and G. Zambelli, *"Decomposing Berge
graphs containing no proper wheels, long prisms or their complements"*,
*Combinatorica*, to appear — as a possible *alternative* to Section 24
(*"Let us mention a theorem of [12], which could be applied at this stage as an
alternative to the next section, the following (and see also [8] for some related
material):"*), and the authors explicitly decline to use it (*"The method we give
below is somewhat shorter than the proof of 23.6 in [12], however."*).  It is
transcribed here like every other numbered statement of the section; see its own
doc-comment.

Section 23 **defines no new term**.  The only definitional material inside it is
an in-proof gloss of the §2 notion *hat* (*"So `Y` contains a hat, that is, there
exists `y' ∈ Y` with no neighbour in `C'` except `z, x₀`"*, inside the proof of
23.2), which occurs in no numbered statement; accordingly
`Workspace.Types.RousselRubio` (where `IsHatForHole` lives) is not imported.
The word *triad* does not occur anywhere in the section.

Every defined term used below is imported and never restated:

* `Workspace.Types.Core` — `IsPathFrom`, `SPGT.interior`, `IsHoleList`,
  `IsAntiholeList`, `holeLength`, `VertexComplete`;
* `Workspace.Types.Wheels` — `IsWheel` (§16's *wheel*);
* `Workspace.Types.WheelSystems` — `OptimalWheel` (§22), `IsFrame`,
  `IsWheelSystem`, `wheelSystemX` (`Xᵢ`), `wheelSystemA` (`Aᵢ`) (all §19);
* `Workspace.Types.Classes` — the classes `F₅, F₈, F₉, F₁₀, F₁₁` of §1;
* `Workspace.Types.Decompositions` — `AdmitsBalancedSkewPartition`;
