* `Workspace.Types.BasicClasses` — `IsLineGraphOfBipartite` (§1), used by 23.6;
* `Workspace.Types.LongOddPrism` — `Recalcitrant` (§13).

Encoding conventions (see `paper/spec/CONVENTIONS.md`):

* a hole is the list `C : List V` of its vertices in cyclic order, its length is
  `holeLength C`, and `V(C)` is `{w : V | w ∈ C}` (so *"`v ∉ V(C)`"* is `v ∉ C`);
* a **cyclically consecutive block** of the hole `C` — the paper's *subpath
  `c₁-c₂-c₃` of `C`*, and its *three consecutive neighbours* — is a prefix of
  some rotation of `C`, `∃ k : ℕ, [c₁, c₂, c₃] <+: C.rotate k`; this is the
  convention already used by `Classes.InF10` and `WheelSystems.IsKite`;
* a path is the list of its vertices in order; `SPGT.interior P` is the paper's
  `P*` (always written qualified — a bare `interior` is Mathlib's topological
  one);
* *"the set of neighbours of `v` in `V(C)`"* is
  `G.neighborSet v ∩ {w : V | w ∈ C}`;
* `Gᶜ` is the paper's `Ḡ`.

**Placement of the "In particular, …" sentences.**  Following the house rule
(`CONVENTIONS.md` §3.7) and the precedent of `Workspace.Statements.S14`
(statement 14.3), the closing sentence of 23.2, 23.4 and 23.5 is genuine
mathematical content and is formalized — as a *separate theorem* in each case
